Gears of War 3 (issue #20 investigation): a native resolve's barrier that returns the source render
target to its previous state is submitted on its own. Batched with the next draw's barrier for the same
render target, it made two transitions of one subresource in one ResourceBarrier call, which the D3D12
debug layer reports (message 1008) thousands of times per run. Legal, but the kind of thing drivers
differ on.

diff --git a/src/graphics/d3d12/render_target_cache.cpp b/src/graphics/d3d12/render_target_cache.cpp
index a781b3a..c953eec 100644
--- a/src/graphics/d3d12/render_target_cache.cpp
+++ b/src/graphics/d3d12/render_target_cache.cpp
@@ -6371,6 +6371,9 @@ void D3D12RenderTargetCache::WriteResolveToTextures(const draw_util::ResolveInfo
   D3D12TextureCache::NativeResolveWriteCounts counts;
   texture_cache.WriteNativeResolveToTextures(write, rt_state, counts);
   command_processor_.PushTransitionBarrier(render_target.resource(), rt_state, rt_state_before);
+  // On its own: otherwise the next draw's barrier for this render target joins the same batch, two
+  // transitions of one subresource in one ResourceBarrier call (D3D12 debug layer warning 1008).
+  command_processor_.SubmitBarriers();
   render_target.SetResourceState(rt_state_before);
 
   native_resolve_written_ += counts.written;
